{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I have trodden.</b> Now this is the answer, the reason: the slaying of Edom and the destruction of the kingdom of Edom." "The meaning of <b>alone.</b> For I decreed thus upon Edom." "<b>And I trampled them.</b> Even though it appears to be future, it is a sign of the standing time [i.e., serves as a temporal indicator]." "<b>And their lifeblood.</b> Now ויז is like ויט משה (Exodus 9:23)." "<b>נצחם</b> is the blood by which a person lives, נצחו, and it is from the root נצח (Isaiah 34:10)." "<b>I have trodden.</b> The alef is in place of the heh of the binyan, and in my opinion it is a word compounded of past and future verb, and the meaning of אגאלתי is like טנוף, like יגאלוהו חשך וצלמות (Job 3:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {2 "Edom is spelled defectively as תורת' in the source; resolved by context.", 4 "כמו ויט appears in the lemma of comment 3 but not in comment 5; rendered consistently."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:47.573990634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}